      "message": "Interesting, I wouldn\u0027t have thought of this approach! Nice.\n\nHowever, with this, we lose the benefits of using Lineage Settings (less code changes to AOSP, like the Settings patch), and instead start going towards the opposite, where it\u0027s needing more code to do it this way, than to just use plain AOSP Settings.\n\nThus, I don\u0027t see any benefit of using a Lineage Setting like this. It\u0027s elegant code, but the maintenance aspect worries me, and I\u0027d be fine with that if there was some benefit to it vs other options.\n\nI\u0027d like to just leave it in the old place in Settings at this point to ship it in a timely fashion, and have the least amount of ongoing maintenance needed.",
